  "interpretation": "Rust has one explicit SaveThread/RestoreThread pair and two epoll_wait entries per query in both orders. C has nine pairs and one poll; Python has 28 pairs and one poll. Scheduler wakeups are approximately one per query for all three. Excess explicit GIL handoff count is not supported as the scalar Rust bottleneck. Poll entry counts do not measure blocking duration or prove redundant waits. No latency savings are inferred.",
